  "claim": "One size past: four junctions (computed exactly on one space: the smallest plain edge-atom space with four junctions that HANDLE-COUNT A's generator gives with four trisums, seed 7 under hash seed 0, with 62 points and six atoms, chosen before its map was computed). Every one of ticket A's frozen statements P1 to P7 holds: yes/no creation reads the atoms and, with the atoms set aside, exactly the four junctions' line pairs block only each other, so four junctions are counted; pair refinement of the native map fixes the atoms, skeleton lines, junction lines, roots, loaded lines, square-mates and leaves; census 6 never creates alone. The map was computed in one fixed point order that keeps at most 19 lines open, and its row 0 equals the solutions of ticket B's enumeration and of the full-memory one.",
